#20005
On the Widmans River~
   To the north lie the poorest parts of the town, where crime and filth
keep most of the citizens away, and many of the guards as well.  Drunks
and beggars wander from alley to alley; the only reason they are still
alive is that they have nothing the thieves want.  The river flows east
toward an archway.
~
