#20008
On the Widmans River~
   The water grows much colder here as a stream from the south pours
into the Widmans River; it must flow out of some sort of cavern.  The
southern bank is so high now that you cannot see the plains at all, but
the cool breeze blowing down into the riverbed reminds you that they are
there.  To the north the mountains loom, some of them shaded by huge
clouds drifting across the sky.  The current pushes your boat east,
though you could move west without too much trouble.
~
