#20015
At the Rock of Pheenix~
   A rock the size of a small mountain stands in the middle of the
river, and the water crashes against it from every side, only to be
turned away.  The rock, named for the greatest priestess to walk the
land in the days before the religious wars, ignores the force of the
water and basks in the sunlight as if nothing could touch it.  Somehow
you manage to avoid crashing into it yourself.  The rapids continue both
east and west.
~
